  "doctrine": [],
  "note": "The Hebrew spelling ends in n before the plural ending. The Akkadian, Ugaritic, Arabic and Syriac comparanda include forms with m. Their use for several members of the Pistacia genus leaves the species of Jacob’s gift open. The place Betonim in Jos.13.26 has its own lexical key."
